secrets/
# Betreiber-eigenes XcodeGen-Overlay: TLS-Pins, gepinnte Hosts,
# Passkey-Relying-Party-Domains und Associated Domains. Verraet, wer die App
# betreibt — darf nie eingecheckt werden. Vorlage: Config/local.example.yml
Config/local.yml

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Snapshots: failure diffs are not committed; reference snapshots are
**/__Snapshots__/_diff_/

# Isolated derivedData for marathon builds
.derived/

# SpeziVibe / agent skills (dev tooling, not app code)
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# H2 (audit v0.16.2) — the generated `HealthLog.xcodeproj/` stays ignored,
# but the SwiftPM lockfile inside its workspace is tracked so the ~50-package
# transitive graph is pinned across clean checkouts / CI / worktree agents
# (a fresh `-resolvePackageDependencies` otherwise resolves "highest
# satisfying" and has already resurrected broken combos — see project.yml
# HealthKitOnFHIR/SpeziLLM notes). XcodeGen does NOT delete this file on
# regen. Git can't re-include a file under an ignored dir without un-ignoring
# every parent segment first, hence the chain below (last-match-wins order,
# and it must sit AFTER the bare `Package.resolved` rule above).
!HealthLog.xcodeproj/
HealthLog.xcodeproj/*
!HealthLog.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/
HealthLog.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/*
!HealthLog.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/
HealthLog.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/*
!HealthLog.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/
HealthLog.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/*
!HealthLog.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/Package.resolved
